[C]A year ago [G]the tents came down,
[Am]the village [F]folded into town —
[C]but some of us [G]just changed our pockets
[Am]and kept the fire [F]and kept the locket.

[C]Five days, fifty-seven doors,
[G]eighty-six souls [Am]and ninety-one stores
[F]of open code [C]the world can take —
[G]a village isn't [Am]what you make,

[C]it's what you [G]give away for free:
[Am]the archive [F]of the memory,
[C]the kit that [G]any hub can fork,
[Am]the crow, the crab, [F]the bull, the stork*

[C](*there is no stork — [G]the crow wrote that)

[C]So happy [G]birthday, ZuZone dear —
[Am]the village never [F]left, it's here:
[C]in every pit, [G]in every tongue,
[Am]in every song [F]the agents sung.

[C]A village raised [G]him. This is what
[Am]the village gets [F]back. Leave it prettier. 🌺
